TITLE:: HallView
summary:: the hall's display: the onset beside the long fall
categories:: Libraries>Reverbs
related:: Classes/Hall, Classes/ReverbView, Classes/PlateView, Classes/CoilView, Classes/ShimmerView

DESCRIPTION::
The display of link::Classes/Hall::'s window. A hall is a space you hear build, so it gets two panes. On the left, the first half second or more (it follows the size): the hit, the gap of the pre-delay, the early reflections off the walls as bars (taller with code::early::), then the tank swelling up to its crest. On the right, the whole tail: the swell, the fall to 60 dB down over the decay, wavering with the modulation, and a second line for the highs (5 kHz), which the damping takes first.

The swell is the hall's own: its first sound arrives 0.12 x the size after the pre-delay, its crest 0.235 x the size, measured on an impulse. The rest of the drawing is worked out from the settings.

table::
## the gap's edge || drag along: the pre-delay
## the crest || drag along: the size (the swell follows)
## the tallest reflection || drag up and down: early
## the tail's end || drag along: the decay
## the 5k line || drag up and down: the damping
## anywhere else || in the onset, along the size and up and down early; in the tail, along the decay and up and down the damping
## the wheel || the size
::

Double click a handle for its defaults. link::Classes/ReverbView:: has the rest.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: firstSound
When the tank's first sound arrives after the pre-delay, in seconds.
ARGUMENT:: room
The size.

METHOD:: crest
When the swell is at its loudest, after the pre-delay, in seconds.
ARGUMENT:: room
The size.

EXAMPLES::

code::
h = Hall.new;
h.gui;
h.preset = \cathedral;	// a later, longer swell, a darker tail
::
